  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://craftcorpus.org/CRAFT_positive_regulator">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://craftcorpus.org/CRAFT_GO_BP_extension_class"/>
    <craft:has_prototypically_entailed_GO_BP_class>http://craftcorpus.org/CRAFT_occurrence_or_attribute_of_positive_regulation</craft:has_prototypically_entailed_GO_BP_class>
    <rdfs:label>positive regulator</rdfs:label>
    <craft:annotatable_text>positive regulator; positive regulators; up regulator; up regulators; upregulator; upregulators; up-regulator; up-regulators</craft:annotatable_text>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>A positive regulator, i.e., something that has a capability of bringing about an occurrence of positive regulation.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  </owl:Class>
  <owl:Class rdf:about="http://craftcorpus.org/CRAFT_reverse_transcription_or_reverse_transcriptase">
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://craftcorpus.org/CRAFT_GO_BP_extension_class"/>
    <craft:has_prototypically_entailed_GO_BP_class>http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GO_0001171</craft:has_prototypically_entailed_GO_BP_class>
    <rdfs:label>reverse transcription or reverse transcriptase</rdfs:label>
    <craft:annotatable_text>RT</craft:annotatable_text>
    <obo:IAO_0000115>An occurrence of reverse transcription, i.e., DNA synthesis process that uses RNA as the initial template for synthesis of DNA, but which also includes an RNase activity to remove the RNA strand of an RNA-DNA heteroduplex produced by the RNA-dependent synthesis step and use of the initial DNA strand as a template for DNA synthesis; or, a reverse transcriptase, i.e., an enzyme capable of catalyzing this process.</obo:IAO_0000115>
  </owl:Class>
